Every gel French tip tutorial you have watched makes it look simple. Your first attempt at home looked nothing like that. That gap is not about skill or tools. It is about missing information, and this is the post that fills it.

<strong>How to do french tip gel nails</strong> at home is genuinely achievable, even if your hands are not naturally steady and even if you have tried before and ended up with lifting edges, streaky tips, or a smile line that seemed to shrink as it dried. The full <strong>how to do french tip gel nails</strong> process is learnable. This tutorial covers all three application methods so you can choose the right one for your tools and skill level, walks through every step including the ones competitors skip, and gives you the fixes you need when something goes wrong mid-process. For a full overview of every French style, <a href='/blog/french-nails/reverse-french-manicure'>start with the complete French manicure guide</a>.

<strong>How to do french tip gel nails</strong> well comes down to four things: correct prep, the right method for your hands, understanding how to cure, and knowing what to do when the tip does not go to plan. All four are covered here.

