## What You Actually Need Before You Start (Kit List That's Honest, Not Overwhelming)

Three products do more to determine your result than anything else: a gel base coat, a white gel polish with good opacity, and a no-wipe top coat. Everything else is application method.

Here is the honest kit list, no fluff, nothing that sends you to buy 14 products before you can start.

**The non-negotiables:**
- LED or UV nail lamp (LED is standard for home use, faster cure, more compact)
- Gel base coat
- Sheer nude or milky pink gel polish (your base colour)
- White gel polish (opacity matters, look for "opaque white" not "sheer white")
- No-wipe gel top coat
- Nail file (180 grit) and buffer (220 grit)
- Nail dehydrator or prep wipe (rubbing alcohol works)
- Lint-free wipes

**For your chosen method, pick one:**
- Silicone nail stamper (beginner-friendly, fast)
- Nail guide stickers / French tip stickers (most consistent curve)
- Fine detail brush or liner brush (freehand method, most control)

One note on <a href='https://www.webmd.com/beauty/features/gel-manicure-safety' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>gel manicure safety</a>: UV exposure from nail lamps is low, but if you prefer caution, apply SPF to your hands before starting or use fingerless UV-protective gloves.

