## Step-by-Step: How to Do Gel French Tips With a Silicone Stamper

The stamper method rewards a single confident press more than tentative repeated touches. Commit to the press.

**What you need:** silicone nail stamper, white gel polish, gel base coat, sheer nude gel, no-wipe top coat, LED lamp

**Steps:**

1. Apply and cure your gel base coat (30 to 60 seconds LED)
2. Apply one thin coat of sheer nude gel polish across the full nail, cure for 60 seconds
3. Apply a second thin coat of nude gel if needed for coverage, cure for 60 seconds, leave the inhibition layer on
4. Load the stamper: dab white gel polish onto the stamper pad, scrape lightly with the scraper card to remove excess, leaving a thin even layer
5. Position the stamper at the tip of the nail with the curve aligned to your desired smile line
6. Press down with even, steady pressure, do not rock the stamper
7. Lift cleanly in one movement
8. **Flash cure immediately**: place that nail under your lamp for 10 to 15 seconds to freeze the tip before moving to the next finger
9. Once all ten nails are stamped and flash cured, do a full cure of 60 seconds on each nail
10. Apply no-wipe top coat across the full nail, sealing the free edge (cap the tip), then cure for 60 seconds

If the tip looks thin or patchy after stamping, wait for the flash cure to set, then load the stamper again and press a second layer over the same position. Two thin stamps beat one heavy press.

For thinner tip variations, lighter stamper pressure deposits less product, creating a narrower line. This is how you control tip width without buying a different tool.

