## Step-by-Step: How to Do Gel French Tips With Guide Stickers

If your last attempt at a French tip ended with one side higher than the other, guide stickers are about to become your favourite tool.

**What you need:** French tip guide stickers / nail guide strips, white gel polish, gel base coat, sheer nude gel, no-wipe top coat, LED lamp

**Steps:**

1. Apply and cure gel base coat (30 to 60 seconds LED)
2. Apply one thin coat of sheer nude gel, cure for 60 seconds
3. Apply a second coat of nude gel if needed, cure for 60 seconds
4. Wait a full minute after the final cure so the surface is completely set and no longer warm, this matters for sticker adhesion
5. Apply a guide sticker strip to each nail at the smile line position, pressing down firmly at the edges so no gel can bleed underneath
6. Apply white gel over the tip area above the sticker, brush from the sticker edge outward, not back and forth
7. **Flash cure for 10 to 15 seconds** before peeling the sticker. this is the step most people skip, and it is the reason tips look ragged when the sticker is removed
8. Peel the guide sticker slowly, pulling back parallel to the nail (not upward) while the gel is still slightly soft
9. Full cure for 60 seconds
10. If the smile line edge looks slightly raised, a very thin layer of top coat will level it, cap the free edge when applying
11. Cure no-wipe top coat for 60 seconds

One coat of white gel may look sheer. this is normal. The opacity of white gel polish depends on pigment load, and most formulas need two thin coats to look truly white rather than milky. Apply a second sticker-guided coat if the first looks translucent. "White gel going streaky" is almost always a one-coat problem, not a product fault.

<a href='https://thegelbottle.com/blog/how-to-do-a-french-manicure-with-gel-polish/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Professional gel application technique</a> uses the same two-coat principle for tips. it is not a beginner error, it is the correct process.

