## How Long Do Gel French Tips Last, and How to Make Them Last Longer

A well-prepped gel French tip lasts two to three weeks. That is not marketing copy. that is the realistic range when prep and curing are both done correctly.

The variables that shorten wear are almost always prep failures: oil left on the nail plate, skipping the dehydrator, base coat applied too thick, or tips not capped at the free edge. "Gel French tips lifting after 5 days" is, in nearly every case, a prep problem rather than a product problem.

**What actually extends wear:**

- Cap the free edge with every coat, not just top coat
- Keep hands out of prolonged water exposure for the first 24 hours after application, gel continues to harden after the lamp
- Apply cuticle oil daily, hydrated skin around the nail reduces lifting at the edges
- Avoid using your nails as tools (opening ring pulls, scraping labels). Tip edge impact is the leading cause of chipping

Gel French tips on short nails wear just as long as on longer lengths, and they are less likely to catch on things and break. The idea that you need length for a French tip to "work" is a myth, a two-millimetre tip on a five-millimetre free edge looks clean and modern. Once you have mastered this look, the <a href='/blog/french-nails/double-french-tip-nails'>double French tip</a> is a natural next step with the same application process.

